  "title": "O Christmas Tree",
  "composer": "Traditional",
  "about": "O Tannenbaum means O fir tree in German. The tune is an old German folk melody, and nobody knows who first wrote it. The Leipzig teacher Ernst Anschütz wrote the words sung today in 1824. His song praises the fir tree for staying green all through the winter.",
  "funFact": "The same tune carries the state song of Iowa, and Maryland's state song used it until 2021.",
